U.S. Chemical Safety and Hazard Investigation Board. *Fatal Liquid Nitrogen Release at Foundation Food Group*, report 2021-03-I-GA, December 2023. Incident: Gainesville, Georgia, 28 January 2021. [Official investigation](https://www.csb.gov/foundation-food-group-fatal-chemical-release-/) · [Complete 116-page report](https://www.csb.gov/file.aspx?DocumentId=6268).

Read the whole report, distinguishing observed evidence, tests, competing explanations, conclusions and recommendations. Its institutional and human account is part of understanding a functioning gas system.

Title, contents, executive findings and selected level-control tests and uncertainty about tube damage were inspected on 30 October 2026. The report establishes the consequence of the displaced bubbler tube but does not establish exactly how or when it was bent. It is an official federal investigation, with credited photographs/materials to retain. No independent accident reconstruction is claimed; recommendations are not presented as a statement of current law. The report stays external.

